In GCP, a 3-tier architecture consists of a VPC with 3 subnets — Web, App, and DB tiers. The Web tier is usually exposed using a Cloud Load Balancer and runs on Compute Engine, GKE, or App Engine. 
The App tier runs on private Compute Engine or GKE behind an Internal Load Balancer. The DB tier is hosted on Cloud SQL or Firestore in a restricted subnet.
Cloud NAT enables secure outbound internet access for private resources. IAM, Secret Manager, Cloud Armor, and Cloud Monitoring provide security and observability.

9)How can we get On prem data to cloud  in gcp cloud?
To move on-prem data to GCP, we can use multiple options based on use case. For secure connectivity, we use Cloud VPN or Cloud Interconnect. 
For bulk migration, we can use Transfer Appliance or Storage Transfer Service to move data into Cloud Storage or BigQuery.
For real-time streaming or CDC, Pub/Sub, Dataflow, and Datastream are commonly used. 
In hybrid environments, VPN or Interconnect ensures a secure link between on-prem and GCP resources.

10)Lambda functions what do they do exactly?
AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service that allows you to run code without provisioning or managing servers. You only pay for the time your code runs.
Runs code when triggered (API call, S3 event, schedule, etc.)
Automatically scales based on requests
Works as backend compute for event-driven applications
Integrates with AWS services like S3, DynamoDB, API Gateway, CloudWatch, etc.
Some scenarios where lambda is used
1)slack / Teams Notification Automation
Scenario: Whenever an EC2 instance’s CPU goes above 75%, notify your DevOps team.
Flow: CloudWatch Alarm triggers Lambda
Lambda formats a message & sends it to Slack/Teams webhook
 Useful for monitoring & incident alerts
2)Developers launch EC2/RDS resources without tags. Tags like Environment, Owner, Cost-Center are required for billing.
CloudTrail event (resource creation) triggers Lambda
Lambda adds mandatory tags automatically
Helps with cost governance & FinOps
3)Auto Backups and Cleanup
Scenario: Take daily snapshots of EC2 volumes and delete older ones after 7 days.
Flow: EventBridge triggers Lambda daily
Lambda takes snapshot of EC2
Deletes snapshots older than 7 days
Saves storage & ensures backup compliance
4)Authentication & Authorization
Scenario: Want to control login using custom logic (JWT, OAuth, AD, OTP)?
Flow: User calls API via API Gateway
Lambda validates user credentials, generates JWT token
AWS Lambda is used for automation, event-driven processing, serverless APIs, monitoring, DevOps tasks, IoT, file processing, and real-time notifications.
It eliminates the need for servers and reduces cost.
Auto-Tagging: CloudTrail event triggers Lambda to tag newly created resources for cost tracking.
AMI & Snapshot Automation: Scheduled backup Lambda takes daily EC2 snapshots and deletes older ones after 7 days.

